---
import { getImage } from "astro:assets"
import lesson from "../../assets/pivo-meet-lesson.webp"
import CaseStudyDemo from "../../components/CaseStudyDemo.astro"
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro"

const [small, medium] = await Promise.all([480, 800].map(width => getImage({ src: lesson, width, format: "webp" })))
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  projectName="Pivo Meet"
  path="/work/pivo-meet/"
  title="Pivo Meet remote coaching lessons with Vue and Agora — Jérôme Schaeffer"
  description="A frontend case study of Pivo Meet at 3i. Try a two-person riding lesson, grant the coach camera control, and follow a simulated cloud recording."
  heading="Coaching a rider with Pivo Meet"
  image={lesson.src}
  imageWidth={lesson.width}
  imageHeight={lesson.height}
  srcset={`${small.src} 480w, ${medium.src} 800w, ${lesson.src} ${lesson.width}w`}
  sizes="(min-width: 1174px) 1080px, (max-width: 500px) calc(100vw - 40px), 92vw"
  imageAlt="The rider fills the guest view in the Pivo Meet demo. The coach’s own preview sits in the lower right corner."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    A coach watching a riding lesson needs to see both horse and rider, even as they cross the arena.
    At 3i, I maintain and extend Pivo Meet, the Vue 3 and Agora web app that lets a coach join a rider by video
    and adjust the camera with the rider’s permission.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    A sample lesson in the portfolio demo, with the coach’s preview tucked into the corner.
    Arena photograph by <a class="text-link" href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/76340031@N02/53003001579/">Jeremy T. Dyer, BLM Utah</a>.
   <a class="text-link" href="/assets/pivo-recording.png">See the recording screen from Pivo’s lesson guide</a>.
  </Fragment>

  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="camera-control">
    <h2 id="camera-control">Who controls the rider’s camera?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        The side-by-side layout gives coach and rider equal space to talk. When the rider sets off, the coach can
        switch to a small self-preview and use most of the screen to watch the horse.
      </p>
      <p>
        Changing the layout only changes the coach’s screen. To move the rider’s Pivo Pod, the rider first
        enables Guest Control. The coach can then hold an arrow to pan or zoom. If the rider withdraws
        permission, movement stops.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="recording">
    <h2 id="recording">When is a lesson recording ready?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        The room timer starts when the participants join. Recording has a separate clock. Choosing Cloud shows
        the available recording time, and the recording counter starts once the recorder is ready.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pressing stop takes the recording through stopping and processing before the app confirms it has been
        saved. Leaving also asks for confirmation, so a coach who presses Leave by mistake can return to the
        lesson with the recording still running.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="demo-section" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <h2 id="demo-title">Try the coach’s controls</h2>
    <p>
      Open the sample lesson, switch to Small preview, and try Camera control. Turn on Guest Control for the
      rider, then hold an arrow to follow the horse. You can also try cloud recording. The demo uses a still
      photograph and simulates the call and recording in your browser.
    </p>
    <CaseStudyDemo demo="meet" label="Open lesson demo" fallback="Enable JavaScript to try the lesson controls." />
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
